# boostlink design guide

Reference page: the homepage (`/`, components in `src/modules/catalog/components/home-*`).
New and redesigned pages must look and behave like it. File ownership rules are in AGENTS.md.

## Brand
- Name: **boostlink**, always lowercase. Tagline: "Apps. Faster together."
- Logo mark: black "b" on a yellow rounded square (app-icon style).
- Two sides of the marketplace: **Creators** and **Apps** (never "advertisers", "brands", "partners").

## Color (use tokens from `src/app/globals.css`, never hardcoded hex in components)
- Default theme: dark. Light theme must work too.
- Yellow `--primary` (#FFD600) is the only accent: primary buttons, active states, key numbers, highlights.
- Text on yellow is always `--primary-foreground` (near black).
- Never use yellow as text on light backgrounds. To emphasize a word, use the marker style:
  yellow highlight behind the word, black text.
- Side colors exist only in illustrations, never in buttons or body text:
  Creators coral (#FF6B4A dark / #E5482A light), Apps violet (#8B5CF6 dark / #7C3AED light),
  as tokens `--side-creators` / `--side-apps` (`bg-side-creators/20`, `bg-side-apps/20`).
- Flat fills. No decorative gradients, glows, blur blobs or "AI-looking" gradient lines.

## Typography
- Font: Plus Jakarta Sans (bundled, `src/app/fonts/plus-jakarta-sans.ttf`). Headings bold with tight letter-spacing; body regular/medium.
- Headlines short (2 lines max). Subtitles max 3 lines on desktop, last line shorter, never a single word.
- Section copy: one or two lines per item. No internal/dev wording in UI text.

## Shape and layout
- Rounded, chunky shapes like the logo: cards ~20px radius, inputs 12px, buttons pill.
- Generous spacing, one clear focal point per section.
- Mobile first: check every change at 375px. No horizontal page scroll. Tables become cards on mobile.
- CTA buttons: 52px tall, yellow primary with arrow; secondary uses Hover Border Gradient.

## Motion
- Calm and purposeful: 300-500ms ease-out, small movements, no bounce or spin.
- Max 2-3 animated elements per page. Prefer CSS (transform/opacity) over JS animation.
- Start animations when in view; pause when off screen.
- Every animation respects `prefers-reduced-motion` (show the final state).

## Components
- Base: shadcn/ui in `src/components/ui`. Forms: `FieldGroup`/`Field` + `useActionState`.
- Already installed effects (reuse before adding new ones): bento-grid, canvas-text (dark mode only),
  layout-text-flip, glowing-effect, hover-border-gradient, infinite-moving-cards, animated-list,
  number-ticker, orbiting-circles.
- New effects come from Aceternity UI or Magic UI via the shadcn CLI (`pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add ...`).

## Content honesty (hard rules)
- No invented people, testimonials, logos, counts, rankings or metrics. Empty states are honest.
- Example numbers in illustrations must be clearly examples and mathematically consistent
  (e.g. 20% of a $39 plan = $7.80). Keep one currency per page.
- Don't promise features that don't exist yet (e.g. click tracking before stage 5).
- One name per thing across the UI (e.g. "Discover apps" everywhere).

## Checks before finishing
- 375px and desktop, light and dark, both toggle versions where relevant.
- Keyboard navigation and visible focus. WCAG AA contrast for every text/background pair.
